/*
 * GENERATED from the stock dtbo entry for this board (msm-id 0x24f) - do not
 * edit by hand.  Regenerate with tools/boot/gen-abl-labels.py.
 *
 * The bootloader resolves every factory dtbo overlay fragment by looking that
 * fragment's label up in this DTB's /__symbols__, then merges the fragment's
 * subtree into the resolved node.  The vendor tree exposes the 129 labels
 * below; a mainline tree has none of them, and one missing label makes the merge
 * fail so the phone returns to fastboot before the kernel runs.
 *
 * Every label therefore gets an empty node inside this isolated container.  The
 * fixups resolve and the ~1.5 MB of vendor content lands here instead of being
 * merged into nodes that describe real hardware - the vendor overlays were
 * compiled against a 1-cell vendor tree, so letting them into our 2-cell nodes
 * produces a structurally inconsistent tree.  The board's own labels were
 * renamed (msm_soc / msm_tlmm / msm_rsc) so these names are free.
 */

